  "result": "\u2705 Done. I've added complete VAT support to invoices:\n\n**VAT Calculation (lineVAT):**\n- VAT per line = (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n- Rounded per line using roundCents()\n- Handles VAT rates of 21%, 9%, and 0% (exempt)\n\n**Updated invoiceTotals:**\n- Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- `vat` = sum of all rounded line VATs\n- `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped to 0)\n\n**Design decision:**\n- VAT is computed **per line** on the taxable amount (after line discount)\n- Each line's VAT is **rounded independently**\n- Invoice VAT is the **sum** of line VATs, never a percentage of invoice total\n- This prevents rounding errors and allows for precise control per line\n\n**Updated renderInvoiceText:**\n- Shows VAT on its own line (just above total) when VAT > 0\n- Skips VAT line when total VAT is 0 (VAT-exempt items)\n- Format: `VAT: \u20acx.xx` followed by `Total: \u20acx.xx`\n\n**Added 12 tests:**\n- lineVAT: calculation, different rates (21/9/0), with discounts, rounding\n- invoiceTotals: VAT inclusion, multiple lines, mixed rates, discounts + VAT\n- renderInvoiceText: VAT display, conditional rendering, line ordering\n\n**Test results:** All 103 tests pass \u2713",
